@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `holE`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.03 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **A long fork and variable stretch follows.** Columns 1 to 26, `yobA` to `manX`, are carried by 87 to 89%, and a branch of 26 persistent families runs through them in 11% {S2.c1-26, S2.b1}. The `man` genes, columns 24 to 26, are [[mannose transport]] {S2.c24-26, Q}. Then columns 27 to 70, `yoaL` to `ydjK`, are variable, carried by 67 to 87%, and a branch of 3 families runs through columns 77 to 79 in 11 to 24% {S2.c27-70, S2.b77}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99 against 93%, and hesitates less there, 0.03 against 0.30 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 70, `ydjK`, is a variable column, at 0.90 bits {H, M}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Columns 77 to 79, `pncA` to `sppA`, are carried by 60 to 82% {S2.c77-79}. The last column is `sppA`, in 60% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.30 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.93 against 0.17 bits, and names fewer genes, 71% against 98% {C}.

